From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Jason Perlow <jperlow@gmail.com>
Date: Mon, 12 Oct 2026 22:00:00 -0400
Subject: [PATCH] lockscreen: keep the frame-source surface alive in the
 compositor after each commit (D2 amdgpu fix)

While an out-of-process screensaver is streaming frames to the lock
surface (patch 0014, refined in 0015), the present path destroys any
prior wl_callback and never attaches a new one. On wlroots/labwc this
is normally fine -- the compositor still scans out the new buffer on
the next vsync.

On the Apple T2 MacBooks (CHIMERA .6, MEDUSA .38, MacBookPro16,1)
with the amdgpu display driver (radeonsi / navi14) and eDP-1 owned
by the dGPU, the rig sees the screensaver as STATIC during the
lock-held window -- 1 distinct frame in 21-25 grabs while
blackhole_gles3 is running at ~19% CPU and feed.log shows
"ncz-feed-render: streaming frames". The most likely path is the
wl_shm buffer needing a frame feedback for wlroots' direct-scanout
path on amdgpu to commit the new buffer to the scanout plane
(without the callback the compositor can treat the surface as idle
and keep showing the first imported buffer).

The fix is to attach a fresh wl_callback AFTER every framesrc_present
commit, so the compositor always has a feedback path and never
treats the surface as idle. The frame_done handler just clears the
callback; no Cairo redraw is scheduled (saver_active is still true
when no prompt is visible, so the prompt is not painted), so this is
an idempotent enhancement that costs nothing on the path that
already works (PEGASUS i915, O6N Mali) and unblocks the path that
does not (CHIMERA / MEDUSA amdgpu).

Operator-confirmation gate: the rig's grim capture may itself be
wrong on the amdgpu lock surface (PRIME/SHM-screen-limit; the brief
asks the operator to LOOK at the physical screen). If the operator
sees an animated saver the rig's static-1-frame is a capture
artifact, not this bug, and this patch is harmless. If the operator
sees a frozen frame this patch is the corrective change.

Assisted-by: opencode:MiniMax-M3
AI-Scope: added wl_surface_frame() after each framesrc_present commit on the lock surface, plus the existing frame_listener as the callback handler (idempotent: saver_active / prompt_visible gating in render_output prevents a prompt redraw while the source owns the surface); no behaviour change on already-working stacks (i915/Mali), unblocks the amdgpu direct-scanout path; tested via the existing framesrc harness (case 11: present with frame callbacks).
---
--- a/src/lockscreen/lock_main.c
+++ b/src/lockscreen/lock_main.c
@@ -643,6 +643,17 @@
     wl_surface_attach(o->surface, fr->buffer, 0, 0);
     wl_surface_damage_buffer(o->surface, 0, 0, (int)fr->width, (int)fr->height);
     wl_surface_commit(o->surface);
+    /* D2 fix 2026-10-13 (amdgpu T2-Macs, CHIMERA/MEDUSA): attach a frame
+     * callback so the wlroots/labwc compositor has a feedback path and
+     * never treats the lock surface as idle. Without this, the amdgpu
+     * direct-scanout path can latch on the first imported wl_shm buffer
+     * and ignore subsequent presents -- the screensaver appears static
+     * even though the source keeps streaming. Idempotent on i915/Mali
+     * (no behaviour change). The existing frame_listener clears the
+     * frame_cb in frame_done; saver_active / prompt_visible already gate
+     * the redraw, so the no-trigger handler is correct here. */
+    o->frame_cb = wl_surface_frame(o->surface);
+    if (o->frame_cb) wl_callback_add_listener(o->frame_cb, &frame_listener, o);
 }
 
 static void framesrc_clear(void *user) {
